WEBVTT

00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:14,520
How long do the rife machine bulbs last? Do they burn out?

00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:21,380
The rife machine bulbs don't burn out.

00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:27,380
So it's not a, it's a gas filled tube.

00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:34,380
So there's nothing to burn out as it could desert light bulb or something like that.

00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:36,380
So they don't burn out.

00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:41,380
However, they can, you know, they can break.

00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:46,380
You can drop the bulb. Typically, if you dropped it just down flat on itself,

00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:49,380
it's not going to break. It's encased in plastic.

00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:56,380
But if you drop it on the end, so those, those electrical cords go into the tube

00:00:56,380 --> 00:01:00,380
and they attach through the glass cylinder in there and that can break.

00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:03,380
The glass inside there can break.

00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:07,380
So if you banged the end of it onto the side of the banner,

00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:12,380
if you dropped it down where the cylinder is going straight down

00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:19,380
and it hit on the end of the tube that can break and then it's broken.

00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:23,380
So that is then going to have to be replaced.

00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:28,380
The other thing that we've seen with some of the bulbs over time,

00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:31,380
especially the older bulbs.

00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:36,380
I mean, people that have had them for several years,

00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:44,380
it can start the cords themselves because it's, you know, electricity going through those cords,

00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:47,380
especially on the older true right bulbs where they were, where they,

00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:54,380
the cords curled around and then were zip tied to the, to the plastic tube.

00:01:54,380 --> 00:02:01,380
You need that, that, that, that burn into the plastic casing of the,

00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:06,380
of the cord, the cord has just gone bad and you can't replace that.

00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:09,380
So the whole bulb just has to be replaced.

00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:14,380
We had, we had several of those actually in the last couple of months

00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,380
where people said there's felt, they smelled, smell coming from that

00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:20,380
and then they noticed the cord was getting really hot.

00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:25,380
If that's the case, you're going to have to replace the tube.

00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:31,380
So the, there's nothing else you could do about that.

00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:35,380
What else can you do to damage the cords on the bulbs?

00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:38,380
So of course you can break the bulb if you really hit it hard.

00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:41,380
You can break the end of the bulb so you look at it.

00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:46,380
You can't see any damage because that is on the end, like I said,

00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:51,380
if you dropped it on the edge and you hit it at just right,

00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:55,380
you could, you could snap the glass in there and all the gas would leak out of the tube

00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:58,380
and you notice it doesn't work.

00:02:58,380 --> 00:03:00,380
It doesn't light up at all anymore.

00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:03,380
We've had that happen a couple of times and then you could burn,

00:03:03,380 --> 00:03:07,380
the cord could burn and that has to be replaced.

00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:11,380
The other thing is the ends of the cord where it plugs into the knife machine,

00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:15,380
especially if you yank on them and don't grab the red or the black

00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:18,380
and carefully, gently wiggle it out.

00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:22,380
If you yank on it or lots of times it's happening where somebody trips

00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:26,380
on the cord and it pulls it out and that can damage that piece

00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:29,380
and then that, that could typically be repaired.

00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,380
Nothing else can be repaired.

00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:38,380
So yeah, so understand our warranty on the bulbs is nonexistent.

00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:42,380
So if something happens to it, it's user error.

00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:47,380
So you're going to have to cover the cost of that repair.

00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:50,380
I mean, if it's a repair on the end of it, it's not such a big deal.

00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:53,380
But if anything else, you just have to replace the bulb.

00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:57,380
So if the bulb comes to you and it works and then something happens

00:03:57,380 --> 00:04:01,380
and it doesn't work, then unfortunately that's going to be on you

00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:03,380
to replace that bulb.

